[MOCK PUBSUB -> 7cb5edfa-0f6d-48a1-bc7e-9a7032a5b909] {'type': 'security_findings', 'summary': 'The security audit of the page https://sqasa.co/contacto/ has been completed. Here are the findings:\n\n### Passive Analysis Findings:\n1. **Missing Security Headers**: The page lacks several important security headers such as Content Security Policy (CSP), X-Content-Type-Options, and X-Frame-Options.\n   - **Severity**: Medium\n   - **Remediation**: Implement these headers to protect against clickjacking, MIME type sniffing, and other attacks.\n\n2. **Insecure Cookies**: Some cookies are not marked as Secure or HttpOnly.\n   - **Severity**: Medium\n   - **Remediation**: Ensure cookies are marked with Secure and HttpOnly flags to prevent interception and access via JavaScript.\n\n3. **Server Information Disclosure**: The server header reveals the server type and version.\n   - **Severity**: Low\n   - **Remediation**: Configure the server to hide version information to reduce the risk of targeted attacks.\n\n### Active Scanning Findings:\n1. **Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) Vulnerability**: Detected in the input fields of the contact form.\n   - **Severity**: High\n   - **Remediation**: Implement input validation and output encoding to prevent execution of malicious scripts.\n\n2. **SQL Injection Vulnerability**: Potential SQL injection points were identified in the form submission.\n   - **Severity**: Critical\n   - **Remediation**: Use parameterized queries and prepared statements to prevent SQL injection attacks.\n\n3. **Open Redirects**: Identified in URL parameters.\n   - **Severity**: Medium\n   - **Remediation**: Validate and sanitize URL parameters to prevent open redirect vulnerabilities.\n\n### Recommendations:\n- **Implement Security Headers**: Add CSP, X-Content-Type-Options, and X-Frame-Options headers.\n- **Secure Cookies**: Ensure all cookies are set with Secure and HttpOnly attributes.\n- **Hide Server Information**: Configure the server to not disclose version information.\n- **Sanitize Inputs**: Use input validation and output encoding to prevent XSS.\n- **Use Parameterized Queries**: Protect against SQL injection by using prepared statements.\n- **Validate URL Parameters**: Prevent open redirects by validating and sanitizing URL parameters.\n\nFor further details on these vulnerabilities, I recommend consulting the OWASP guidelines. If you need more information on any specific vulnerability, please let me know!', 'findings_count': 12}
