\n   - **Reference**: [OWASP CSRF](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/csrf)\n\n2. **Open Redirects**\n   - **Description**: The application allows open redirects, which can be exploited for phishing attacks.\n   - **Remediation**: Validate and restrict redirect URLs to a whitelist of trusted domains.\n   - **Reference**: [OWASP Open Redirect](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Open_redirect)\n\n### Low Vulnerabilities\n1. **Information Disclosure**\n   - **Description**: The application discloses server version information in HTTP headers.\n   - **Remediation**: Remove or obfuscate version information in headers.\n   - **Reference**: [OWASP Information Disclosure](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Information_Leakage)\n\n2. **Directory Listing**\n   - **Description**: Directory listing is enabled, exposing sensitive files.\n   - **Remediation**: Disable directory listing on the server.\n   - **Reference**: [OWASP Directory Listing](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Directory_indexing)\n\n### Next Steps\n- Prioritize fixing critical and high vulnerabilities immediately.\n- Implement a regular security review process to catch and fix vulnerabilities early.\n- Consider using automated security tools for continuous monitoring.\n\nFor further details on each vulnerability, consult the OWASP guidelines linked in the references.', 'findings_count': 21}
